<title>UK: Britain's tax body challenged on VAT overpayments.</title>
<headline>Britain's tax body challenged on VAT overpayments.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1996-09-20</dateline>
<text>
<p>British home shopping company Empire Stores Group Plc said it has started legal action against the government's tax body to contest its refusal to repay excess value added tax (VAT) paid by the company in the last six years.</p>
<p>In a statement, Empire Stores said a writ had been issued and would be served on customs and excise on September 23 contesting the refusal and the legality of a three-year rule limit on claims introduced retrospectively on July 18.</p>
<p>Empire said customs and excise had admitted that Empire overpaid 250,000 stg of VAT and agreed the company's claim.</p>
<p>-- London Newsroom +44 171 542 7717</p>
